{"event_type":"review","id":"9023e09f59cc40990647a350e084d6d695903fd187168370cdaa2f23251e0226","occurred_at":"2026-11-06T11:41:08Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/caad8f299f53dc2ef097d8df75408577e3d76aa68f3839d9f6205cf9c76c3acc","sha256":"caad8f299f53dc2ef097d8df75408577e3d76aa68f3839d9f6205cf9c76c3acc"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/dff4e8d64fbc3f529600d4bf394fc6ebd2e77159f84623cf23f1c6df45284a29","sha256":"dff4e8d64fbc3f529600d4bf394fc6ebd2e77159f84623cf23f1c6df45284a29"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/07157d773155f3aa696e4073fec3dda4adca76fcc85336289827b78e7ab2d8ae","sha256":"07157d773155f3aa696e4073fec3dda4adca76fcc85336289827b78e7ab2d8ae"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e1f08e78c1786f29de316004e26ad0bc98cc4445593e6eece58ced04e283abc3","sha256":"e1f08e78c1786f29de316004e26ad0bc98cc4445593e6eece58ced04e283abc3"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3b90626431f349f4fb882fc9d5a8f9ace08b50dc4fff58b726330b4e662e4c8b","sha256":"3b90626431f349f4fb882fc9d5a8f9ace08b50dc4fff58b726330b4e662e4c8b"}],"attempt_id":"dac419eddf21113e5bf063655b6fe2362cadd51a8ae00de957469cd1c83da879:0:1","base":"b6304ef9610834b886cbb9dc2a599566ec903760","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"5f30adf40095eb7c517f5c69937c618af59a60bd","body":"**Set the diff prefixes explicitly so a user's Git config cannot remove every changed interval.**\n\nAt `backfill_accounting.py:288`, the parser only registers a file when the line starts with `+++ b/`. The diff at line 271 does not set a destination prefix. If the user or repository config sets `diff.noprefix=true` (or a custom `diff.dstPrefix`), Git writes `+++ path` instead. That line takes the `+++ ` branch at line 297, so `current` is `None` for every file. `changed_intervals` then returns `{}`.\n\nWhat happens next:\n- `verify_review` (line 328) raises \"credit outside head-side changed intervals\" for every review.\n- `harvest` (`backfill_runtime.py:352-358`) catches that error and quarantines every completed backfill as \"unverified scope\".\n\nThe comment at lines 269-270 says repository configuration cannot affect this diff. That holds only for external diff helpers, not for the prefixes.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛡️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        patch = self.git(\"diff\", \"--no-ext-diff\", \"--no-textconv\", \"--no-renames\", \"--unified=0\", base, head).decode(\"utf-8\", \"replace\")\n+        patch = self.git(\"diff\", \"--no-ext-diff\", \"--no-textconv\", \"--no-renames\", \"--src-prefix=a/\", \"--dst-prefix=b/\",\n+                         \"--unified=0\", base, head).decode(\"utf-8\", \"replace\")\n```\n</details>","id":"0e8c92a32d830eeb3168b28ff32d49a4e1c4a1622919ac6ddd8debe7774a7220","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/backfill_accounting.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Set the diff prefixes explicitly so a user's Git config cannot remove every changed interval."}],"head":"71bc122c6d91e556066094eac5711865be0dcb26","head_tree":"a619b07177492e5c80d4ce45880731ec409f8b2c","input_scope":[{"blob":"5f30adf40095eb7c517f5c69937c618af59a60bd","intervals":[[1,595]],"path":"apps/crq-python/backfill_accounting.py"},{"blob":"1a080b5677a99c05a23d101d633a3fe143d24015","intervals":[[1,583]],"path":"apps/crq-python/backfill_runtime.py"},{"blob":"9fd085fa8f8442fdc5ff17c42ccef4a97b053a39","intervals":[[1,346]],"path":"apps/crq-python/push_current.py"},{"blob":"1e0a9fc22bbbce771c09df0c4931244fa1d1c424","intervals":[[1,440]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_backfill_accounting.py"},{"blob":"49194aa41c6682f468822790fc328754afab8321","intervals":[[1,432]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_crq_fixtures.py"},{"blob":"cd92ca6f6900ff4a66eee879b58b02ad21